From: tb322fc bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] mangoapp: pause while the Steam UI is focused and the overlay is game-only

With STEAM overlay level > 0 but "show overlay in Steam" disabled,
steamclient still reports the HUD as active (no no_display in the
config), while gamescope sets GAMESCOPE_FOCUSED_APP_GFX=769 for the
focused Steam UI.  msg_read_thread computed steam_focused and render()
suppressed the HUD content, but new_frame was never cleared, so the
main loop kept doing full-rate empty ImGui/present/X11 work (~10% CPU
on SM8750).

Suppress new_frame while steam_focused (unless perf logging is active)
so the main loop takes the paused path (hidden window, 0.5 s sleep).
It resumes on the first frametime of a focused game.
---

diff --git a/src/app/main.cpp b/src/app/main.cpp
--- a/src/app/main.cpp
+++ b/src/app/main.cpp
@@ -218,6 +218,19 @@
                         steam_focused = false;
                     }
 
+                    /* With "show overlay in Steam" disabled, the HUD draws
+                     * nothing while the Steam UI is focused, but new_frame
+                     * still kept the main loop doing full-rate empty renders
+                     * (ImGui + present + X11 round trips), costing ~10% CPU.
+                     * Suppress new_frame (and clear a pending one) so the main
+                     * loop takes the paused path (hidden window, 0.5 s sleep).
+                     * It resumes on the first frametime of a focused game. */
+                    if (steam_focused && !logger->is_active()){
+                        std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lk(mangoapp_m);
+                        new_frame = false;
+                        should_new_frame = false;
+                    }
+
                     if (msg_size > offsetof(mangoapp_msg_v1, latency_ns))
                         gamescope_frametime(mangoapp_v1->app_frametime_ns, mangoapp_v1->latency_ns);
 
